India Voice Platform — Phase 2 Implementation Plan

 Context

 The voice prototype is confirmed working (user tested
 it — AI voice spoke, user's voice was captured
 correctly). The codebase has:
 - ✅ Full voice worker (LiveKit v1.13.7 + Sarvam
 STT/TTS + Silero VAD) — working
 - ✅ Production-grade PostgreSQL schema (8 tables,
 RLS, triggers, billing math library)
 - ✅ Redis + LiveKit in Docker compose
 - ✅ Static landing page + setup guide (2 web pages)
 - ✅ API health/readiness endpoints only (2
 endpoints)
 - ❌ No auth, no business endpoints, no real
 dashboard, no campaigns, no billing

 Goal: implement the product milestone by milestone
 per the file document. Preserve working voice
 prototype throughout.

 Working voice config (must not change):
 - LiveKit server: v1.13.7, JS client 2.17.0, Agents
 1.8.1
 - STT: Sarvam STTRealtime / Saaras:v3-realtime
 - TTS: Sarvam Bulbul:v3
 - LLM: Groq openai/gpt-oss-20b with
 reasoning_effort="low", include_reasoning=False
 - Browser uses text-stream transcription (not legacy
 transcription events)

 ---
 Milestone 1 — Stabilize Voice Baseline (30 min)

 Mostly done from previous session. Two small
 remaining items:

 1. Update apps/web/app/setup/page.tsx — the "Voice
 implementation waits for your review" checkpoint
 panel still says D3 is pending. Change to reflect it
 is now implemented and working, with startup
 commands.
 2. Verify infra/compose.yaml --keys format —
 currently "${LIVEKIT_API_KEY:-devkey}: ${LIVEKIT_API_
 SECRET:-devsecret-which-must-be-at-least-32-chars}".
 Test that Docker Compose variable substitution
 produces a valid key: secret string. Fix if the
 format is wrong.

 No voice worker changes.

 ---
 Milestone 2 — Authentication and Organizations

 Auth provider: Clerk (recommended — managed OIDC,
 best Next.js SDK, free for early stage, matches
 auth_issuer/auth_subject DB column design). Requires
 free Clerk account.

 Alternative if user prefers no external account:
 Better-Auth (open source, self-hosted).

 NestJS API changes (apps/api/src/)

 New modules/files:
 - auth/ — JWT middleware verifying Clerk JWKS;
 @CurrentUser() decorator; RolesGuard
 - organizations/organizations.controller.ts +
 organizations.service.ts — POST /orgs (provision org
 + wallet on first sign-in), GET /orgs/me
 - users/users.controller.ts + users.service.ts — GET
 /users/me, PATCH /users/me
 - agents/agents.controller.ts + agents.service.ts —
 CRUD for reusable voice agent configurations

 All endpoints use withTenantTransaction from
 packages/database for RLS context. JWT guard on all
 business routes.

 New dependencies to add to apps/api/package.json:
 jwks-rsa, passport-jwt, @nestjs/passport

 Database migration

 packages/database/drizzle/0002_agent_configs.sql —
 new agent_configs table:
 - id, org_id (FK), name, language enum, voice
 (speaker name), instructions_text, created_at,
 updated_at
 - RLS + grants matching existing table pattern from
 0001_tenant_security.sql

 Next.js changes (apps/web/)

 - Install @clerk/nextjs
 - apps/web/middleware.ts — protect /dashboard/*,
 redirect unauthenticated to /sign-in
 - apps/web/app/(auth)/sign-in/[[...sign-in]]/page.tsx
 — Clerk embedded sign-in
 - apps/web/app/(auth)/sign-up/[[...sign-up]]/page.tsx
 — Clerk sign-up
 - Update apps/web/app/layout.tsx with <ClerkProvider>
 - Add NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY +
 CLERK_SECRET_KEY to env

